Subject: [PATCH 30/38] =?UTF-8?q?feat(qwen3-tts):=20cooperative=20cancel?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20shouldCancel=20per-frame=20poll=20+=20worker=20c?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ancel=20protocol=20(re-port=2064185fa,=20spec=20#7)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Runtime: TalkerGenerationRequest gains an optional shouldCancel poll, threaded
through PerBatchStreamingHandler and checked once per decoded frame in
runTalkerGenerationLoop (post-sample, pre-EOS — the v0.8.x insertion point).
A tripped batch is marked finished and its ChunkEmitter flushes immediately
with isFinal=true (flushFinal is now idempotent so the loop-exit flush pass
stays a no-op). Unset shouldCancel = upstream behavior, unchanged.

Worker: restores the v0.8.0 cancelMap protocol — cancel line trips the slot's
atomic flag, cancel_ack{tripped} is emitted synchronously from the reader
thread, the stream ends with the is_final=true chunk, and a `cancelled`
event replaces `done` (exact v0.8.0 event names/fields; voxedge
_WorkerIO.cancel consumes them unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
